+# ADIPS Web — Development Patch Tracker
+
+Companion to *ADIPS Web Development Plan & Developer Document*.
+The build is delivered as **small sequential patches** (one chat reply each).
+Each patch is a `git apply`-able file; this document is updated by every patch.
+
+## 1. Workflow
+
+```bash
+cd adips_web
+git checkout -b feature/adips-web          # once (plan section 14)
+git checkout -b feature/web-<module>       # per patch
+git apply --index /path/to/000N-<name>.patch
+flutter pub get                            # only needed when pubspec changed
+flutter analyze && flutter test
+flutter run -d chrome
+git commit -m "Patch 0N: <name>"
+```
+
+Rules every patch follows: stays small enough for one reply; shared code is
+**copied from `adips_app` by `tools/sync_shared.sh`** (not retyped, so no
+business-logic drift); UI-only code lives under `lib/web/`; this file is updated.
+
+## 2. Findings from the audit (Phase 0)
+
+| # | Finding | Impact | Handled in |
+|---|---------|--------|-----------|
+| 1 | `adips_web` was the untouched Flutter counter template | Everything built from scratch | Patch 01 |
+| 2 | `pubspec.yaml` had `assets:` **outside** `flutter:` | No asset was registered | Patch 01 (fixed) |
+| 3 | Backend has **no CORS middleware** (`gin.Default()` only) | A browser on another origin cannot call the API at all | Patch 02 (backend patch B01) |
+| 4 | Mobile `AdipsHttpHelper` authenticates by setting a `Cookie` header | Browsers forbid scripts from setting `Cookie` → every call would be 401 | Patch 02: web client sends `Authorization: <jwt>` (backend middleware already accepts this fallback, raw token, no `Bearer`) |
+| 5 | Mobile uses GetX for state **and** navigation (`Get.offAllNamed`, `Get.snackbar`) | Controllers that navigate/toast can't be copied verbatim | Reuse services/models as-is; adapt controllers (router/toast via web adapters) |
+| 6 | Backend base URL is Render free tier (cold start 20–50 s) | Needs long first-load timeouts and a clear "waking up" state | Patch 02 |
+| 7 | Theme references font `Poppins` but no font is bundled in `adips_app` | Falls back to the default font on both platforms | Open question (§6) |
+
+Backend API (all under `/api/v1`, envelope `{success,message,data,meta?}`):
+users (signup, login, logout, validate), accounts (CRUD, summary, reorder,
+archive/unarchive, delete-preview, adjust), transactions (CRUD, summary),
+transfers (by group UUID), categories (CRUD, reorder), transaction-types
+(CRUD), settings (get/patch).
+
+## 3. Decisions
+
+| Decision | Choice | Why |
+|----------|--------|-----|
+| State / DI | GetX (`get`, `get_storage`) | Same as mobile → shared controllers/services reusable |
+| Routing | `go_router` with a `ShellRoute` | Real URLs, deep links, refresh-safe, persistent sidebar (plan §7, §10) |
+| Notifications | `ScaffoldMessenger` snackbars (Patch 03+) | `Get.snackbar` needs `GetMaterialApp`, which conflicts with `go_router` |
+| Shared code | Copy via `tools/sync_shared.sh`, import rewrite `package:adips/utils/theme→adips_web/core/theme`, `…/constants→core/constants` | Plan §9 "reuse, don't duplicate" without a package refactor of the mobile repo |
+| Default theme | Dark (persisted toggle) | Plan §8: dark is the primary identity. Mobile follows system — change `ThemeController` if you want parity |
+| Icons | Material icons in the shell | Mobile barely uses iconsax; avoids an extra dependency |
+
+## 4. Patch roadmap & status
+
+Sizing target: one patch ≈ 8–15 authored files, ≤ ~900 authored lines.
+
+| Patch | Name | Plan phase | Repo | Status |
+|-------|------|-----------|------|--------|
+| **01** | Web foundation: theme, responsive shell, routing, placeholders | 0, 1 | web | ✅ **Delivered** |
+| 02 | Core networking: models + services sync, web HTTP client, session storage, **backend CORS (B01)** | 1/2 | web + backend | ⬜ Next |
+| 03 | Authentication: login, register, onboarding, route guard, real logout | 2 | web | ⬜ |
+| 04 | Dashboard A: total balance, summary stat cards, account cards | 3 | web | ⬜ |
+| 05 | Dashboard B: date/sort filters, search, recent transactions | 3 | web | ⬜ |
+| 06 | Transactions list/table with search, filter, sort, pagination | 4 | web | ⬜ |
+| 07 | Add/edit transaction dialog, details page, delete confirm | 4 | web | ⬜ |
+| 08 | Transfers: form dialog + validation | 5 | web | ⬜ |
+| 09 | Accounts: list + add/edit dialog (icon/colour/type/currency) | 6 | web | ⬜ |
+| 10 | Accounts lifecycle: archive, default, adjust balance, delete preview, reorder | 6 | web | ⬜ |
+| 11 | Categories: list, filter by type, add/edit, icon/colour, reorder | 7 | web | ⬜ |
+| 12 | Transaction types | 7 | web | ⬜ |
+| 13 | Settings + Profile + about/version | 8 | web | ⬜ |
+| 14 | Responsive/accessibility QA fixes, overflow pass | 9 | web | ⬜ |
+| 15 | Release: env config, build, deploy rewrite rules, smoke checklist | 10 | web | ⬜ |
+
+Plan §13 immediate tasks → Patch 01 covers tasks 1–5 (baseline, dependency
+comparison, shared theme/constants, WebShell, responsive routing). Tasks 6–11
+map to Patches 03–15.
+
+## 5. Patch 01 — Web foundation  ✅
+
+**Adds**
+- `pubspec.yaml`: `get`, `get_storage`, `go_router`, `flutter_web_plugins`; assets block fixed.
+- `web/index.html`, `web/manifest.json`: ADIPS branding, dark boot background, viewport.
+- `tools/sync_shared.sh` (group `theme`) → copied `lib/core/constants/{adips_palette,sizes,image_strings,text_strings}.dart` and `lib/core/theme/**` (20 files, imports rewritten, otherwise identical to mobile).
+- `lib/core/responsive/breakpoints.dart` (768 / 1200), `lib/core/theme/theme_controller.dart`, `lib/core/constants/web_assets.dart`.
+- `lib/routes/app_routes.dart`, `app_router.dart`: all plan routes, `/` → `/dashboard`, 404 page, no-transition shell pages.
+- `lib/web/layout/`: `web_shell`, `web_sidebar` (full / icon-rail / drawer), `web_header` (title, Add menu, theme toggle, profile menu), `responsive_layout`, `nav_items`.
+- Placeholders: every module page shows "built in Patch NN"; `/login`, `/register`, `/onboarding` are temporary stubs.
+- `test/widget_test.dart`: breakpoints, nav matching, sidebar widget test (replaces the template counter test).
+
+**Temporary items to remove later**
+- `_logout` in `web_shell.dart` just navigates to `/login` → Patch 03.
+- `AuthPlaceholderPage` "Continue to dashboard" button → Patch 03.
+- `PagePlaceholder` usages → replaced module by module.
+
+**Hosting note (path URLs):** the app uses `/dashboard`, not `/#/dashboard`.
+Your host must rewrite unknown paths to `index.html` (Patch 15 adds exact
+Render/Netlify/Firebase rules). `flutter run -d chrome` already does this.
+
+**Verification checklist**
+- [ ] `flutter pub get && flutter analyze && flutter test`
+- [ ] Chrome ≥1200px: full sidebar, items highlight, URL changes, refresh keeps the page
+- [ ] 768–1199px: icon rail with tooltips · <768px: hamburger opens drawer
+- [ ] Theme toggle switches and survives reload
+- [ ] `/transactions/42` shows "Transaction #42"; `/nonsense` shows the 404 page
+
+> Honesty note: this environment had no Flutter SDK, so Patch 01 was checked
+> statically only (all imports resolve, brackets balanced, patch applies
+> cleanly to a fresh clone) — **not compiled**. If `flutter analyze` reports
+> anything, paste it and I'll fix it first in the next reply.
+
+## 6. Open questions
+
+1. Poppins: bundle the font in both apps (recommended) or accept the fallback?
+2. Default web theme: dark (current) or follow system like mobile?
+3. Deploy target (Render static site, Netlify, Firebase, other)? Affects Patch 15 and the CORS allow-list in Patch 02.
+
+## 7. Change log
+
